module engine where

-- =========================================================================
-- invert.fenel — backward constraint propagation (abstract interpretation),
-- the BACKWARD dual of `propagate`'s forward transfer.
-- unified-static-analysis Phase 3b-2 (brief:
-- `workstreams/unified-static-analysis/briefs/phase-3b-2-invert-backward-transfer.md`).
--
-- THE PORT (the inference hot-path, slice 2). Given `output = inputs[0] op
-- inputs[1]` with all but `inputs[unknownIdx]` known, solve the unknown's
-- constraint over the SetExpr lattice — equation solving. Binary arithmetic
-- only (`inputs.length != 2` ⇒ $all); invertible only for + - * / (and the
-- enum pointwise of those); % and every non-arith op ⇒ $all (uninvertible).
-- Exact-integer interval admission widens numeric intervals beyond native
-- numbers. Their endpoints no longer justify scalar arithmetic inverses, so
-- interval branches abstain with SeAll; native-number enum inversion remains.
--
-- decide-substrate Phase 1 Stage E: the internal `Sm*` SetMarker vocabulary is
-- RETIRED — this body reads / builds the canonical registered `$tag` `Se*`
-- SetExpr directly (a real ADT a `.fenel` body pattern-matches on), reusing
-- propagate.fenel's `seTag` / `loOf` / `hiOf` / `numBound` adapters (the old
-- `.tag`-string dispatch + interval-nesting + marshalBound guard) and its
-- interval/enum helpers. The TS delegate (`invert.ts`) now passes SetExpr
-- through `setExprToTag` (dual-read normalize) instead of the deleted
-- `marshalSet` round-trip; ~342 LOC of legacy backward-transfer decision logic
-- was retired, Fenel up.
--
-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- REUSE OF propagate.fenel (the D-3b-1 "shared low-level helpers" north-star,
-- realized — D-3b-2-2). `invert` is structurally a mirror of `propagate`:
-- same interval/enum marker algebra, same Maybe-bound machinery. The interval
-- inverse arms are propagate helpers verbatim:
--   invertAdd      ≡ propSubIv output known        (output - known)
--   invertSubLeft  ≡ propAddIv output known        (a = output + b)
--   invertSubRight ≡ propSubIv known  output       (b = a - output)
--   invertDivLeft  ≡ propBinaryArith "*" output known  (a = output * b — forward multiply)
-- Only `invertMul` (the DIVISION corners output / known) is genuinely new, and
-- it reuses propCornerMinMax / mkSmInterval / the propLoNeg/propHiPos/
-- propZeroIncl zero-guards — only the corner VALUES (division, not
-- multiplication) and the corner builder differ. The enum pointwise inverse
-- (`invertSolveArith` / `invertEnum`) mirrors propArithVal / propEnumArith
-- with the unknownIdx left/right asymmetry, reusing dedupeValues + the
-- nested-loop shape.
--
-- ±INFINITY (the propagate precedent). Fenel has no infinity literal; bound
-- arithmetic branches on Just / Nothing. A DIVISION corner output/known is
-- finite ⟺ the output bound is present (Just) AND the known bound is either
-- unbounded (Nothing ⇒ finite/∞ = 0) or a present NON-ZERO value (a zero
-- divisor corner ⇒ ∞ ⇒ excluded, matching the legacy Number.isFinite filter —
-- and Fenel `div x 0 = 0` not ∞, so the zero is caught explicitly). An
-- output-unbounded corner is always non-finite ⇒ excluded (∞/x = ∞ or NaN).
--
-- SIGNED ZERO (the ONE documented divergence from the legacy byte-output). The
-- legacy TS leaked IEEE signed zero into a bound value: `finite / -Infinity =
-- -0`. Fenel has a SINGLE zero — the runtime's `num x = Number x || 0`
-- canonicalizes −0 → +0 (−0 is falsy), and a typed `: Number` return collapses
-- it — so the finite/±∞ corner is +0 here where the legacy carried −0. This is
-- a JS-representation artifact, NOT a language-conceptual value (−0 === 0, so
-- it is semantically identical and invisible to every downstream set
-- operation); the parity test canonicalizes ±0 before comparing. Reproducing
-- −0 faithfully is impossible without disabling the runtime's num-coercion, and
-- would be the wrong call: the pure-ADT view of a numeric bound has one zero.
--
-- THE `known`-UNION DISTRIBUTION WRINKLE (the TS `withKnown(k)`): the top-level
-- TS `invert` distributes over a `$union` not only in `output` (like the
-- forward path) but also in `known`, REBUILDING the inputs array. Here the core
-- recursion operates on (op, output, known, unknownIdx) directly — the UNKNOWN
-- input is never read (only its index matters, for the idx asymmetry) — so the
-- `withKnown` rebuild is subsumed by recursing with each union branch `k` as
-- the new `known`. The arity/idx guards + the known-of-inputs extraction live
-- in the dispatched `invert` entry.
--
-- NO ENTITY DECLS (the assignable.fenel / propagate.fenel audit-green
-- invariant): the markers are plain records, reused from 3b-1 — entity + law
-- count move +0, the audit stays exit-0. Engine FNS are safe (law +0, lock +0).
-- =========================================================================


-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- invert — the dispatched entry. Arity/idx guards, then the known extraction
-- + the canonical SetExpr fold. The TS delegate canonicalizes output + the two
-- inputs at the boundary and normalizes the canonical result.
-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

@label "Invert"
@description "Backward type propagation (abstract interpretation): given `output = inputs[0] op inputs[1]` with all but `inputs[unknownIdx]` known, compute the constraint on the unknown input over the canonical SetExpr lattice. Binary only (inputs.length != 2 ⇒ SeAll); + - * / retain the native-number enum inverse with the unknownIdx left/right asymmetry for - and /. Interval branches abstain with SeAll because interval membership admits exact integer records that raw scalar arithmetic does not preserve. % and every non-arith op ⇒ SeAll. Consumes and authors the registered Se* ADT directly; the TS delegate only canonicalizes boundary inputs and applies the final normalize."
@tags "engine" "invert" "inference" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3b-2"
invert : (op: String) -> (output: a) -> (inputs: b) -> (unknownIdx: Number) -> c
invert op output inputs unknownIdx =
  if invertBadArity inputs unknownIdx then SeAll
  else invertCore op output (invertKnownOf inputs unknownIdx) unknownIdx

@label "invert: bad arity?"
@description "True when the inputs are not exactly a binary pair, or the unknownIdx is neither 0 nor 1 — the uninvertible-arity guard (⇒ SeAll). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "invert" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3b-2"
@category "engine-internal"
invertBadArity : (inputs: a) -> (unknownIdx: Number) -> Bool
invertBadArity inputs unknownIdx =
  if neq (length inputs) 2 then True
  else if propAnd (neq unknownIdx 0) (neq unknownIdx 1) then True
  else False

@label "invert: known of inputs"
@description "The KNOWN input marker: inputs[1] when the unknown is index 0, else inputs[0] (the other side). Assumes a binary pair (the arity guard ran). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "invert" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3b-2"
@category "engine-internal"
invertKnownOf : (inputs: a) -> (unknownIdx: Number) -> b
invertKnownOf inputs unknownIdx =
  case head inputs of
    Nothing -> SeAll
    Just in0 ->
      case tail inputs of
        Nothing -> SeAll
        Just rest ->
          case head rest of
            Nothing -> SeAll
            Just in1 -> if eq unknownIdx 0 then in1 else in0


-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- invertCore — the marker fold over (output, known, unknownIdx). The UNKNOWN
-- input is never read (only its index, for the - / / asymmetry), so the TS
-- `withKnown` union-rebuild is subsumed by recursing with each branch as the
-- new `known`. Keep absorption and union distribution before the carrier fence:
-- $none absorb → $all output →
-- distribute over $union in output → distribute over $union in known →
-- interval in either operand ⇒ $all → enum×enum → $all.
-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

@label "invert: core fold"
@description "The backward-transfer marker fold over (output, known, unknownIdx): $none in either ⇒ $none; $all output ⇒ $all; distribute over a $union in output OR in known; any interval operand ⇒ $all (its inhabitants need not be native numbers); enum×enum ⇒ the pointwise inverse; otherwise $all. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "invert" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3b-2"
@category "engine-internal"
invertCore : (op: String) -> (output: a) -> (known: a) -> (unknownIdx: Number) -> b
invertCore op output known unknownIdx =
  if eq (seTag output) "SeNone" then SeNone
  else if eq (seTag known) "SeNone" then SeNone
  else if eq (seTag output) "SeAll" then SeAll
  else if eq (seTag output) "SeUnion" then SeUnion { branches = map (\s -> invertCore op s known unknownIdx) output.branches }
  else if eq (seTag known) "SeUnion" then SeUnion { branches = map (\k -> invertCore op output k unknownIdx) known.branches }
  else if eq (seTag output) "SeInterval" then SeAll
  else if eq (seTag known) "SeInterval" then SeAll
  else if propAnd (eq (seTag output) "SeEnum") (eq (seTag known) "SeEnum") then invertEnum op output.values known.values unknownIdx
  else SeAll


-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- interval inverse — the backward transfer over Maybe bounds. + - * / reuse
-- the propagate.fenel interval arithmetic where they coincide (the mirror
-- identities above); only invertMul (division corners) is new.
-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

@label "invert: interval inverse"
@description "Interval inverse admission fence: SeAll for every op. Numeric endpoints do not restrict interval inhabitants to native numbers; admitted exact integer records do not follow the raw scalar arithmetic that the retained corner helpers model. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "invert" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3b-2"
@category "engine-internal"
invertIv : (op: String) -> (output: a) -> (known: a) -> (unknownIdx: Number) -> b
invertIv op output known unknownIdx = SeAll

@label "invert: interval mul-inverse (division corners)"
@description "Multiplication's interval inverse admission fence: SeAll. The known interval can admit exact integer records that raw multiplication coerces to zero, so endpoint division cannot constrain the unknown soundly. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "invert" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3b-2"
@category "engine-internal"
invertMul : (output: a) -> (known: a) -> b
invertMul output known = SeAll

@label "invert: division corners"
@description "The four division corners of output / known, in the order (oL/kL, oL/kH, oH/kL, oH/kH), keeping only the finite ones. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "invert" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3b-2"
@category "engine-internal"
invertMulCorners : (oLo: a) -> (oHi: a) -> (kLo: a) -> (kHi: a) -> b
invertMulCorners oLo oHi kLo kHi =
  let l1 = appendItem (invertDivCorner oLo kLo) []
  let l2 = appendItem (invertDivCorner oLo kHi) l1
  let l3 = appendItem (invertDivCorner oHi kLo) l2
  let l4 = appendItem (invertDivCorner oHi kHi) l3
  propCollectJusts l4 []

@label "invert: division corner"
@description "One division corner oBound / kBound: an unbounded output bound ⇒ Nothing (∞/x non-finite, excluded); a present output bound over an unbounded known bound ⇒ Just{ 0, exclusive } (finite/±∞ = ±0; the Fenel runtime canonicalizes to the single +0 — signed zero is a JS-repr artifact, `num x = Number x || 0` collapses −0, so the legacy IEEE −0 becomes +0 here, semantically identical since −0 === 0; the parity test canonicalizes ±0); over a zero known value ⇒ Nothing (finite/0 = ∞, excluded — Fenel `div` returns 0 on a zero divisor, so the zero is caught explicitly); over a present non-zero known value ⇒ Just{ quotient, both inclusive }. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "invert" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3b-2"
@category "engine-internal"
invertDivCorner : (oBound: a) -> (kBound: a) -> b
invertDivCorner oBound kBound =
  case oBound of
    Nothing -> Nothing
    Just o ->
      case kBound of
        Nothing -> Just { value = 0, inclusive = False }
        Just k -> if eq k.value 0 then Nothing else Just { value = div o.value k.value, inclusive = propAnd o.inclusive k.inclusive }

@label "invert: interval div-inverse right (b = a / output)"
@description "Right-operand division's interval inverse admission fence: SeAll. Interval membership does not justify native-number endpoint division across its broader admitted carriers. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "invert" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3b-2"
@category "engine-internal"
invertDivRight : (output: a) -> (known: a) -> b
invertDivRight output known = SeAll


-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- enum (pointwise) inverse — the idx-asymmetric scalar solver + the nested
-- loop + dedupe (mirrors propEnumArith).
-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

@label "invert: enum inverse"
@description "Pointwise enum inverse: for every numeric (o, k) solve the unknown via invertSolveArith (idx asymmetry), keeping defined + finite results, then dedupe (first-seen). Empty ⇒ SeNone. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "invert" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3b-2"
@category "engine-internal"
invertEnum : (op: String) -> (ovals: a) -> (kvals: a) -> (unknownIdx: Number) -> b
invertEnum op ovals kvals unknownIdx =
  let raw = invertEnumOuter op ovals kvals unknownIdx []
  if eq (length raw) 0 then SeNone
  else SeEnum { values = dedupeValues raw [] }

@label "invert: enum inverse outer"
@description "Outer loop of the enum×enum pointwise inverse — over the output values. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "invert" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3b-2"
@category "engine-internal"
invertEnumOuter : (op: String) -> (ovals: a) -> (kvals: a) -> (unknownIdx: Number) -> (acc: a) -> a
invertEnumOuter op ovals kvals unknownIdx acc =
  case head ovals of
    Nothing -> acc
    Just o ->
      let acc2 = if isNumber o then invertEnumInner op o kvals unknownIdx acc else acc
      case tail ovals of
        Nothing -> acc2
        Just rest -> invertEnumOuter op rest kvals unknownIdx acc2

@label "invert: enum inverse inner"
@description "Inner loop of the enum×enum pointwise inverse — over the known values for a fixed output value. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "invert" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3b-2"
@category "engine-internal"
invertEnumInner : (op: String) -> (o: a) -> (kvals: a) -> (unknownIdx: Number) -> (acc: a) -> a
invertEnumInner op o kvals unknownIdx acc =
  case head kvals of
    Nothing -> acc
    Just k ->
      let acc2 = if isNumber k then invertEnumOne op o k unknownIdx acc else acc
      case tail kvals of
        Nothing -> acc2
        Just rest -> invertEnumInner op o rest unknownIdx acc2

@label "invert: enum inverse one"
@description "Solve one (o, k) for the unknown, appending the result when defined (not ÷0 / %-undefined) and finite. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "invert" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3b-2"
@category "engine-internal"
invertEnumOne : (op: String) -> (o: a) -> (k: a) -> (unknownIdx: Number) -> (acc: a) -> a
invertEnumOne op o k unknownIdx acc =
  case invertSolveArith op o k unknownIdx of
    Nothing -> acc
    Just r -> if numberIsFinite r then appendItem r acc else acc

@label "invert: scalar solve"
@description "Solve `output = unknown op known` (idx 0) or `output = known op unknown` (idx 1) for the scalar unknown ⇒ Just result, undefined cases ⇒ Nothing. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "invert" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3b-2"
@category "engine-internal"
invertSolveArith : (op: String) -> (output: a) -> (known: a) -> (unknownIdx: Number) -> b
invertSolveArith op output known unknownIdx =
  if eq unknownIdx 0 then invertSolveLeft op output known
  else invertSolveRight op output known

@label "invert: scalar solve (idx 0)"
@description "Solve output = unknown op known: + ⇒ output - known; - ⇒ output + known; * ⇒ output / known (known 0 ⇒ Nothing); / ⇒ output * known; % and other ⇒ Nothing (not uniquely invertible). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "invert" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3b-2"
@category "engine-internal"
invertSolveLeft : (op: String) -> (output: a) -> (known: a) -> b
invertSolveLeft op output known =
  if eq op "+" then Just (sub output known)
  else if eq op "-" then Just (add output known)
  else if eq op "*" then (if eq known 0 then Nothing else Just (div output known))
  else if eq op "/" then Just (mul output known)
  else Nothing

@label "invert: scalar solve (idx 1)"
@description "Solve output = known op unknown: + ⇒ output - known; - ⇒ known - output; * ⇒ output / known (known 0 ⇒ Nothing); / ⇒ known / output (output 0 ⇒ Nothing); % and other ⇒ Nothing. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "invert" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3b-2"
@category "engine-internal"
invertSolveRight : (op: String) -> (output: a) -> (known: a) -> b
invertSolveRight op output known =
  if eq op "+" then Just (sub output known)
  else if eq op "-" then Just (sub known output)
  else if eq op "*" then (if eq known 0 then Nothing else Just (div output known))
  else if eq op "/" then (if eq output 0 then Nothing else Just (div known output))
  else Nothing


-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- interval-output × enum-known distribution — each numeric known value as a
-- point interval, transferred through the interval inverse, unioned. Empty ⇒
-- SeAll (NOT SeNone — mirrors the TS `parts.length ? union : $all`).
-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

@label "invert: interval × enum-known"
@description "Interval-output × enum-known admission fence: SeAll. Point-lifting a native enum value does not restrict the output interval or unknown value to native-number carriers. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "invert" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3b-2"
@category "engine-internal"
invertIvEnumKnown : (op: String) -> (output: a) -> (kvals: a) -> (unknownIdx: Number) -> b
invertIvEnumKnown op output kvals unknownIdx = SeAll

@label "invert: interval × enum-known parts"
@description "Build the union branches of the interval-output × enum-known distribution (the interval inverse applied to each numeric known value as a point interval). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "invert" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3b-2"
@category "engine-internal"
invertIvEnumParts : (op: String) -> (output: a) -> (kvals: a) -> (unknownIdx: Number) -> (acc: a) -> a
invertIvEnumParts op output kvals unknownIdx acc =
  case head kvals of
    Nothing -> acc
    Just v ->
      let acc2 = if isNumber v then appendItem (invertIv op output (propPointIv v) unknownIdx) acc else acc
      case tail kvals of
        Nothing -> acc2
        Just rest -> invertIvEnumParts op output rest unknownIdx acc2


-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- invertConfidence — arithmetic abstains because the API omits the desired
-- output. The retained enum inverse computation is independent of this
-- classifier; its candidate must still be checked against the actual output.
-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

@label "Invert confidence"
@description "Classify a backward-propagation step from its known operand. Arithmetic confidence is unavailable: the API carries no desired output, which might be an interval requiring inverse abstention even when the known input is a finite native-number enum. Finite enum inverse computation remains available. Preserve approximate for an interval-free known union under the remaining non-arithmetic classifications; intervals, bad arity, % / cat, $all and unsupported known shapes are unavailable."
@tags "engine" "invert" "inference" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3b-2"
invertConfidence : (op: String) -> (inputs: a) -> (unknownIdx: Number) -> String
invertConfidence op inputs unknownIdx =
  if invertBadArity inputs unknownIdx then "unavailable"
  else if invertUninvertibleOp op then "unavailable"
  else invertConfOf op (invertKnownOf inputs unknownIdx)

@label "invert: uninvertible op?"
@description "True for the ops invert never inverts: % (not uniquely invertible) and cat (string concat). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "invert" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3b-2"
@category "engine-internal"
invertUninvertibleOp : (op: String) -> Bool
invertUninvertibleOp op = if eq op "%" then True else eq op "cat"

@label "invert: confidence of known"
@description "Arithmetic ⇒ unavailable because the desired output is absent from this API. For the remaining classifications, $all or any interval branch ⇒ unavailable; an interval-free $union ⇒ approximate; otherwise unavailable. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "invert" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3b-2"
@category "engine-internal"
invertConfOf : (op: String) -> (known: a) -> String
invertConfOf op known =
  if propIsArith op then "unavailable"
  else if eq (seTag known) "SeAll" then "unavailable"
  else if invertHasInterval known then "unavailable"
  else if eq (seTag known) "SeUnion" then "approximate"
  else "unavailable"

@label "invert: has interval branch?"
@description "True for an interval or a union with an interval branch, recursively. Tracks the interval inverse admission fence through known unions without changing other confidence classifications. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "invert"
@category "engine-internal"
invertHasInterval : (known: a) -> Bool
invertHasInterval known =
  if eq (seTag known) "SeInterval" then True
  else if eq (seTag known) "SeUnion" then gt (length (filter (\branch -> invertHasInterval branch) known.branches)) 0
  else False

@label "invert: confidence (interval/enum known)"
@description "Interval/enum confidence admission fence: unavailable. Arithmetic inversion needs the desired output to justify its precision, and this API carries no output. The finite native-number enum inverse itself remains available. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "invert" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3b-2"
@category "engine-internal"
invertConfIvEnum : (op: String) -> (known: a) -> String
invertConfIvEnum op known = "unavailable"

@label "invert: is * or /?"
@description "True for the multiplication / division ops (the zero-in-denominator guard applies to these). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "invert" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3b-2"
@category "engine-internal"
invertIsMulDiv : (op: String) -> Bool
invertIsMulDiv op = if eq op "*" then True else eq op "/"

@label "invert: zero in denominator?"
@description "True when the known operand admits zero: an interval whose lo ≤ 0 and hi ≥ 0 (unbounded counts as ∓∞), or an enum containing 0. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "invert" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3b-2"
@category "engine-internal"
invertZeroDenom : (known: a) -> Bool
invertZeroDenom known =
  if eq (seTag known) "SeInterval" then propAnd (invertLoNonPos (loOf known)) (invertHiNonNeg (hiOf known))
  else if eq (seTag known) "SeEnum" then valueMember 0 known.values
  else False

@label "invert: lo ≤ 0?"
@description "True when a lo bound is ≤ 0 (unbounded ⇒ −∞ ⇒ True). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "invert" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3b-2"
@category "engine-internal"
invertLoNonPos : (mb: a) -> Bool
invertLoNonPos mb =
  case mb of
    Nothing -> True
    Just x -> lte x.value 0

@label "invert: hi ≥ 0?"
@description "True when a hi bound is ≥ 0 (unbounded ⇒ +∞ ⇒ True). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "invert" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-3b-2"
@category "engine-internal"
invertHiNonNeg : (mb: a) -> Bool
invertHiNonNeg mb =
  case mb of
    Nothing -> True
    Just x -> gte x.value 0
